# The standard mods' files are listed in catalogue/mods.json by the SHA-256 and size of their working-tree bytes
# (standard_mods_listed), and the client downloads the committed bytes from GitHub: checked out as committed (LF),
# never converted to CRLF (Windows with core.autocrlf), so both describe the same bytes.
crates/vana-client/assets/mods/** -text
# The generated Lua API stubs are compared byte for byte with `vana-client lua-stubs` output (LF) by
# committed_stubs_current; a CRLF checkout (Windows with core.autocrlf) would fail it.
crates/vana-client/assets/mods/library/vana.lua text eol=lf
